{
    "chapter_num": 4,
    "verses_count": 11,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Jonah’s Anger"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But it displeased Jonah exceedingly, and he was angry. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he prayed to the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "SMALL_CAPS",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and said, “I pray thee, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "SMALL_CAPS",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": ", is not this what I said when I was yet in my country? That is why I made haste to flee to Tarshish; for I knew that thou art a gracious God and merciful, slow to anger, and abounding in steadfast love, and repentest of evil. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Therefore now, O "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "SMALL_CAPS",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": ", take my life from me, I beseech thee, for it is better for me to die than to live.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "SMALL_CAPS",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " said, “Do you do well to be angry?” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Jonah went out of the city and sat to the east of the city, and made a booth for himself there. He sat under it in the shade, till he should see what would become of the city."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Jonah Is Reproved"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "SMALL_CAPS",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " God appointed a plant,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Heb qiqayon, probably the castor oil plant"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and made it come up over Jonah, that it might be a shade over his head, to save him from his discomfort. So Jonah was exceedingly glad because of the plant."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Heb qiqayon, probably the castor oil plant"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But when dawn came up the next day, God appointed a worm which attacked the plant,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Heb qiqayon, probably the castor oil plant"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " so that it withered. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When the sun rose, God appointed a sultry east wind, and the sun beat upon the head of Jonah so that he was faint; and he asked that he might die, and said, “It is better for me to die than to live.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But God said to Jonah, “Do you do well to be angry for the plant?”"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Heb qiqayon, probably the castor oil plant"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " And he said, “I do well to be angry, angry enough to die.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "SMALL_CAPS",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " said, “You pity the plant,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Heb qiqayon, probably the castor oil plant"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " for which you did not labor, nor did you make it grow, which came into being in a night, and perished in a night. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And should not I pity Nin′eveh, that great city, in which there are more than a hundred and twenty thousand persons who do not know their right hand from their left, and also much cattle?”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}